    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d396-a1">

                <pb facs="0589" n="469" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg469"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign Affairs to Chargé
                    Dodge.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-12-12"><hi rendition="#italic">December 12,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, referring to his excellency the ambassador’s note of the 6th
                    September last, has the honor to inform Mr. H. Percival Dodge, chargé d’affaires
                    of the United States of America, that Hans Wilhelm Peters, now serving in
                    Infantry Regiment Graf Bose (1st Thuringian) No. 31, was, at his own request
                    readmitted to Prussian allegiance by the Royal Prussian Regierungs-Präsident at
                    Schleswig on the 11th April, 1903.</p>
                <p>Since Peters is therefore a German his request made through the embassy for
                    release from military service can not be acceded to.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails himself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mühlberg</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
